--- body ---
## Context

During the 0181 sweep all 4 of 4 `qwen/qwen3.5-flash-02-23` records hit
`finish_reason=length` at 35K–38K completion tokens, with the sweep cap
at `max_tokens=32768`:

```
run=2 wall=288s  finish=length ctok=36071
run=3 wall=837s  finish=length ctok=35467
run=4 wall=285s  finish=length ctok=38490
run=5 wall=840s  finish=length ctok=35363
```

Bimodal wall time (285s vs 840s) suggests OpenRouter routes to multiple
upstream providers with very different latencies. Two of those four wall
times (837s, 840s) exceed the 600s SIGALRM timeout, causing the
worker-wedge pathology that ticket 0183 also addresses.

The model is otherwise reasonable — same family as the other Qwen
entries — but is the **oldest generation** in the journal set's Qwen
column. All other Qwen entries are 3.6:

```
qwen/qwen3.6-27b
qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b
qwen/qwen3.5-flash-02-23    ← only 3.5
qwen/qwen3.6-plus
qwen/qwen3-max
qwen/qwen3.6-max-preview
```

Replacing it with the newer `qwen/qwen3.6-flash` (verified live on
OpenRouter 2026-05-20 `/api/v1/models`) brings the family to all-3.6
and may also resolve the verbosity issue. Provider metadata:

```
qwen/qwen3.6-flash
  context_length: 1000000
  max_completion_tokens: 65536
  pricing: $0.1875/Mtok in, $1.125/Mtok out
  architecture: text+image+video → text (Qwen3 tokenizer)
```

Note pricing: 3.6-flash is ~3x more expensive per output token than the
3.5 snapshot ($1.125/Mtok vs $0.40/Mtok). Sweep cost increment for 5
reps × ~$0.02 each = ~$0.05 extra.

## Decision

**Replace, not augment.** Same role in the journal set — Qwen mid-tier
Flash MoE — different generation. Keep `qwen3.5-flash-02-23` in
models.yaml (project policy "never delete entries") but comment it out
of journal set use.

## Smoke test required before commit

Before landing the journal-set change, smoke-test `qwen/qwen3.6-flash`
with the locked Experiment 1 prompt config (no_web_search system
instruction, prompt_modules=[], seed=42, max_tokens=32768,
temperature=0.0). Pass criteria:

- API call succeeds, no schema/auth errors.
- `finish_reason=stop` on at least one of two smoke calls (not 4/4
  length like qwen3.5-flash). If 3.6-flash also hits length on this
  prompt, this ticket flips to "raise max_tokens for Qwen-Flash to
  65536" instead, since the model swap alone doesn't fix the issue.
- Wall time under 600s consistently (so the SIGALRM-wedge pathology
  doesn't apply).

Smoke evidence belongs in this ticket log before the journal-set edit
ships.

## Actions

1. **Smoke test** `qwen/qwen3.6-flash` on the locked Experiment 1
   prompt. 2 calls minimum. Record finish_reason, completion_tokens,
   wall_seconds. If smoke fails per the criteria above, do NOT swap —
   re-evaluate as "raise max_tokens for Qwen-Flash" instead.
2. **models.yaml**: add `qwen/qwen3.6-flash` entry with verified prices
   from OpenRouter (see above). Mirror the YAML shape of adjacent Qwen
   entries (provider Alibaba, country CN, architecture moe,
   size_class TBD-likely-medium, context_window 1000000).
3. **models.yaml**: comment out `qwen3.5-flash-02-23` entry with date
   and reason. Do not delete (project policy).
4. **experiments.toml** `[sets.modelset_ablation_journal]`: replace
   `"qwen/qwen3.5-flash-02-23"` with `"qwen/qwen3.6-flash"`. Set
   stays at 17.
5. **post-0181 cleanup**: discard the 4 existing `qwen3.5-flash-02-23`
   records under `outputs/ablation/direct/p1_base/`. Their replacements
   on the 3.6-flash slug land in a tiny follow-up sweep (5 reps × $0.02
   each ≈ $0.10).
6. Note in 0181's closing log entry that the Qwen Flash reps came from
   3.6-flash per 0184, not 3.5-flash-02-23 as originally listed in
   PR #341.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Smoke evidence for `qwen/qwen3.6-flash` recorded in this log:
      finish_reason, ctok, wall_s for at least 2 calls
- [ ] `models.yaml` has new `qwen/qwen3.6-flash` entry with verified
      prices
- [ ] `qwen3.5-flash-02-23` commented out in `models.yaml` with date +
      reason
- [ ] Journal set replaces 3.5 with 3.6; still 17 models
- [ ] 4 stale 3.5-flash records deleted from outputs/p1_base/
- [ ] 5 fresh 3.6-flash reps run; ≥4 of 5 finish_reason=stop
- [ ] measurements.jsonl rebuilt; 3.6-flash records present with
      `prompt_version="p1_base"`, `seed=42`
- [ ] 0181 closing log entry references 0184
- [ ] 0178 manuscript annex notes the chain

## Notes

- Related to 0182 (deepseek-flash swap) and 0183 (httpx timeout). The
  three together pre-empt most of the wedge and truncation pathologies
  exposed by 0181. 0184 is the "Qwen verbose" arm.
- If smoke shows 3.6-flash is just as verbose, the registered fallback
  is "raise per-model max_tokens to 65536 in models.yaml for Qwen Flash
  entries." That requires a small harness change to read per-model
  max_tokens overrides (currently sweep-only via JobSpec). Out of scope
  here unless the smoke says so.
- A more drastic fallback if even 65K truncates: drop the Flash entry
  from the journal set entirely. The Qwen column would have 5 entries
  instead of 6. Manuscript story unchanged (still covers Qwen frontier
  to Qwen mid-tier).
